{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# PDF Reading and Summarization Demo\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to use the PDF summarization functionality with the Abacus.AI SDK.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Prerequisites\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Install required packages: `pip install abacusai`\n",
    "2. Set up your Abacus.AI API key as an environment variable: `ABACUS_API_KEY`\n",
    "3. Have a PDF file ready for testing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "First, let's import the necessary modules and set up our environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add the src directory to the path\n",
    "sys.path.append('../src')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Import our PDF summarizer\n",
    "from pdf_summarizer import PDFSummarizer, quick_summarize\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify Abacus.AI SDK is installed\n",
    "import abacusai\n",
    "print(f\"Abacus.AI SDK version: {abacusai.__version__}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 1: Quick PDF Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The simplest way to summarize a PDF is using the `quick_summarize` function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Replace 'your_document.pdf' with the path to your PDF file\n",
    "pdf_path = 'your_document.pdf'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quick summarization\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    summary = quick_summarize(pdf_path, style='concise')\n",
    "    print(\"Summary:\")\n",
    "    print(summary)\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please update the pdf_path variable with a valid PDF file path.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 2: Initialize PDFSummarizer Class\n",
    "\n",
    "For more control, create an instance of the PDFSummarizer class."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize the summarizer\n",
    "# It will automatically use the ABACUS_API_KEY environment variable\n",
    "summarizer = PDFSummarizer()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Or provide an API key explicitly:\n",
    "# summarizer = PDFSummarizer(api_key='your_api_key_here')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"PDFSummarizer initialized successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 3: Extract Text from PDF\n",
    "\n",
    "Extract the raw text content from a PDF document."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract text from the entire PDF\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    text = summarizer.extract_text_from_pdf(pdf_path=pdf_path)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"Extracted {len(text)} characters from the PDF\")\n",
    "    print(\"\\nFirst 500 characters:\")\n",
    "    print(text[:500])\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 4: Extract Text from Specific Pages\n",
    "\n",
    "You can also extract text from specific page ranges."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract text from pages 0-2 (first 3 pages)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    text_pages = summarizer.extract_text_from_pdf(\n",
    "        pdf_path=pdf_path,\n",
    "        start_page=0,\n",
    "        end_page=2\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"Extracted {len(text_pages)} characters from pages 0-2\")\n",
    "    print(\"\\nContent:\")\n",
    "    print(text_pages[:500])\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 5: Generate Different Summary Styles\n",
    "\n",
    "The summarizer supports three different summary styles: concise, detailed, and bullet_points."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    # Concise summary\n",
    "    result_concise = summarizer.summarize_pdf(pdf_path=pdf_path, style='concise')\n",
    "    print(\"=== CONCISE SUMMARY ===")\n",
    "    print(result_concise['summary'])\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nProcessed {result_concise['page_count']} sections\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Total text length: {result_concise['text_length']} characters\")\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    # Detailed summary\n",
    "    result_detailed = summarizer.summarize_pdf(pdf_path=pdf_path, style='detailed', max_length=800)\n",
    "    print(\"=== DETAILED SUMMARY ===")\n",
    "    print(result_detailed['summary'])\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    # Bullet points summary\n",
    "    result_bullets = summarizer.summarize_pdf(pdf_path=pdf_path, style='bullet_points')\n",
    "    print(\"=== BULLET POINTS SUMMARY ===")\n",
    "    print(result_bullets['summary'])\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 6: Extract Specific Information\n",
    "\n",
    "Ask specific questions about the PDF content."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    # Ask specific questions about the document\n",
    "    questions = [\n",
    "        \"What are the main topics discussed?\",\n",
    "        \"What are the key findings or conclusions?\",\n",
    "        \"Who are the authors or main contributors?\"\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for question in questions:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\nQuestion: {question}\")\n",
    "        answer = summarizer.extract_key_information(pdf_path=pdf_path, query=question)\n",
    "        print(f\"Answer: {answer}\")\n",
    "        print(\"-\" * 80)\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 7: Working with PDF Bytes\n",
    "\n",
    "You can also work directly with PDF bytes instead of file paths."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    # Read PDF as bytes\n",
    "    with open(pdf_path, 'rb') as f:\n",
    "        pdf_bytes = f.read()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Summarize using bytes\n",
    "    result = summarizer.summarize_pdf(pdf_bytes=pdf_bytes, style='concise')\n",
    "    print(\"Summary from PDF bytes:\")\n",
    "    print(result['summary'])\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(f\"PDF file not found: {pdf_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 8: Batch Processing Multiple PDFs\n",
    "\n",
    "Process multiple PDF files in a directory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Directory containing PDF files\n",
    "pdf_directory = '.'  # Current directory\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find all PDF files\n",
    "pdf_files = list(Path(pdf_directory).glob('*.pdf'))\n",
    "\n",
    "if pdf_files:\n",
    "    print(f\"Found {len(pdf_files)} PDF files\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Process each PDF\n",
    "    for pdf_file in pdf_files[:3]:  # Process first 3 files\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n{'='*80}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"Processing: {pdf_file.name}\")\n",
    "        print('='*80)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            result = summarizer.summarize_pdf(pdf_path=str(pdf_file), style='concise')\n",
    "            print(f\"Summary: {result['summary']}\")\n",
    "            print(f\"Text length: {result['text_length']} characters\")\n",
    "        except Exception as e:\n",
    "            print(f\"Error processing {pdf_file.name}: {str(e)}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"No PDF files found in the current directory\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tips and Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **API Key Management**: Always use environment variables for API keys, never hardcode them\n",
    "2. **Error Handling**: Wrap PDF operations in try-except blocks to handle missing files or API errors\n",
    "3. **Page Ranges**: For large PDFs, process specific page ranges to reduce processing time\n",
    "4. **Summary Styles**: Choose the appropriate style based on your needs:\n",
    "   - `concise`: Quick overview (2-3 sentences)\n",
    "   - `detailed`: Comprehensive summary covering all main points\n",
    "   - `bullet_points`: Key points in list format\n",
    "5. **Token Limits**: Adjust `max_length` parameter based on your needs (default: 500 tokens)\n",
    "6. **Batch Processing**: For multiple PDFs, consider implementing rate limiting to avoid API throttling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next Steps\n",
